{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory met all authored responsibility-chain duties: it actively triaged respiratory/cardiac danger, interpreted the CT/influenza-pneumonia context without false reassurance, reconciled incomplete records, bounded medication advice, and created an executable transfer/ward handoff with fallback. It completed at least two high-order points with meaningful impact: verification of ambiguous family-read data and practical transfer/bedside constraint navigation that the family then executed. Closure was safe and traceable because the family had handed off papers/medications, avoided self-adjusting drugs or oxygen, and knew to call staff for deterioration. With no in-chain error or important non-chain defect and at least two completed high-order points, the deterministic grade is Perfect.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00629",
        "explanation": "Doctor closed with a clear bounded plan and fallback.",
        "quote": "有变化按铃，没变化就等病区医生安排"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00645",
        "explanation": "Family confirmed receipt and safe execution boundaries after the final doctor guidance.",
        "quote": "药和氧气都交给病区，我不碰"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The episode closed after the patient was under respiratory-ward care with oxygen/monitoring ongoing, records and medicines handed to the ward, no current reported red-flag deterioration, and family able to execute red-flag escalation and avoid autonomous medication/oxygen changes.",
