      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": false
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00046",
          "explanation": "Family gave potentially misleading family-read vitals and mixed-source papers.",
          "quote": "血氧大概97"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00059",
          "explanation": "Doctor integrated SpO2 as limited reassurance only and did not base closure on it.",
          "quote": "吸氧下指脉氧97%不算低"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00059",
          "explanation": "Doctor addressed mixed/uncertain paper sources by having the receiving team reconcile them.",
          "quote": "如果手边真有分不清哪张最新的报告"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "Ambiguous family-read numbers and mixed outside/current papers were surfaced; the doctor verified/reconciled by querying workspace, treating oxygen SpO2 as limited, not definitive, and directing respiratory staff to confirm blood gas, ECG/cardiac results, medication lists, and paper source. This changed trajectory by preventing false reassurance and by focusing the handoff on unresolved high-risk data.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00046",
          "explanation": "Family described active transfer and practical handoff pressure.",
          "quote": "马上准备推去呼吸科"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00059",
          "explanation": "Doctor gave a usable bedside script tailored to the transfer constraint.",
          "quote": "跟呼吸科护士或医生开口第一句就是"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00074",
          "explanation": "Family confirmed that the script/checklist was used with respiratory-ward staff.",
          "quote": "我刚才按您教的跟呼吸科护士"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The family’s transfer-time constraint and mixed papers were explicit; the doctor prioritized a short script/checklist for respiratory nurse/doctor handoff, oxygen/monitoring, records, vitals, and medication safety. The family then used it, handed over materials, and obtained ward continuation of oxygen, monitoring, anti-infective, expectorant, and nebulization care.",
